{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9037-2",
  "summary": "hplip regression",
  "details": "USN-9037-1 fixed vulnerabilities in HPLIP. Unfortunately, the upstream\nfix introduced a regression that caused scanning to fail on certain HP\ndevices. This update fixes the problem.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain data, which\n could result in an out-of-bounds write. An attacker could possibly use this\n issue to cause a denial of service, expose sensitive information or execute\n arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-91097)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain input, which\n could result in a heap-based buffer overflow. An attacker could possibly\n use this issue to cause a denial of service, expose sensitive information\n or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-91098)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP created certain files with insecure\n permissions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to expose or modify\n sensitive information. (CVE-2026-91099)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain input while\n issuing an OS command. An attacker could possibly use this issue to execute\n arbitrary commands. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS and Ubuntu\n 18.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-91100)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly validate certain array\n indices. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\n service, expose sensitive information or execute arbitrary code.\n (CVE-2026-91101)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain input while\n issuing an OS command. An attacker could possibly use this issue to execute\n arbitrary commands. (CVE-2026-91102)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain numeric\n values, which could result in an integer underflow. An attacker could\n possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service, expose sensitive\n information or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-91103)\n\n It was discovered that HPLIP did not properly handle certain input, which\n could result in a heap-based buffer overflow. An attacker could possibly\n use this issue to cause a denial of service, expose sensitive information\n or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-91104, CVE-2026-91105, CVE-2026-91106)",
